@page "/docs/rtl"

<DocsPage Title="RTL" Description="Right-to-left support for Blazix components.">
    <p>
        Blazix components support right-to-left (RTL) layouts. Text alignment, positioning, keyboard navigation and directional
        styles follow the reading direction for languages like Arabic, Hebrew, and Persian.
    </p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="card-rtl" Direction="rtl" HideCode="true" PreviewClass="h-auto" Caption="A card component in RTL mode." />
    <p>
        When you add components to a project set up for RTL, the CLI turns physical positioning classes into logical ones, so the
        components work in both left-to-right and right-to-left layouts.
    </p>

    <DocsHeading Title="Get Started" />
    <Steps>
        <Step>Set up the project for RTL</Step>
        <p>For a new project, pass <code>--rtl</code> to <code>init</code>. It sets <a href="/docs/blazix-json#rtl"><code>"rtl": true</code></a> in <code>blazix.json</code>.</p>
        <CliCommand Args="init --rtl" />
        <p>For a project that already has components, migrate them. See <a href="#migrating-existing-components">Migrating existing components</a>.</p>
        <Step>Set the direction on the page</Step>
        <p>Put <code>dir</code> and <code>lang</code> on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> in <code>App.razor</code>. The layout, keyboard navigation and popup placement all read the direction from there.</p>
        <CodeFigure Code="@HtmlCode" Title="Components/App.razor" LineNumbers="true" />
        <Step>Add the direction provider</Step>
        <p>
            Some things are decided while rendering, where there&apos;s no CSS to read: which way a Tabs or Navigation Menu indicator
            moves, and which way the arrow keys go in a Calendar. Wrap the app in a <a href="/docs/components/direction">DirectionProvider</a>
            to tell them.
        </p>
        <CliCommand Args="add direction" />
        <CodeFigure Code="@ProviderCode" Title="Components/Routes.razor" LineNumbers="true" />
    </Steps>

    <DocsHeading Title="How it works" />
    <p>With <code>"rtl": true</code> in <code>blazix.json</code>, <code>add</code> rewrites the classes of each component as it copies it, the way shadcn/ui&apos;s CLI does:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Physical classes become logical ones: <code>ml-2</code> becomes <code>ms-2</code>, <code>pr-4</code> becomes <code>pe-4</code>, <code>left-0</code> becomes <code>start-0</code>, <code>rounded-l-lg</code> becomes <code>rounded-s-lg</code>, <code>border-r</code> becomes <code>border-e</code> and <code>text-left</code> becomes <code>text-start</code>.</li>
        <li>Classes with no logical form get an <code>rtl:</code> twin: <code>-translate-x-1/2</code> gets <code>rtl:translate-x-1/2</code>, and <code>cursor-w-resize</code> gets <code>rtl:cursor-e-resize</code>.</li>
        <li>Popups on a logical side slide in from it: <code>data-[side=inline-end]:slide-in-from-left-2</code> becomes <code>slide-in-from-start-2</code>.</li>
        <li>Directional icons (chevrons, arrows) turn around under <code>rtl:rotate-180</code>.</li>
        <li>Context Menu and Dropdown Menu submenus open on <code>Side.InlineEnd</code> instead of <code>Side.Right</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Where the side is physical, classes stay physical: a sheet with <code>Side="SheetSide.Left"</code> keeps its border on its right edge, and a
        tooltip on <code>Side.Left</code> keeps its arrow on the right. Tailwind 4&apos;s <code>space-x-*</code> and <code>divide-x-*</code> already follow
        the direction, so they&apos;re left as they are.
    </p>
    <p>Without <code>"rtl": true</code>, components are copied with physical classes, as before.</p>

    <DocsHeading Title="Sides" />
    <p>
        Popups take a logical side: <code>Side.InlineStart</code> and <code>Side.InlineEnd</code> follow the reading direction, and the popup&apos;s
        <code>data-side</code> keeps saying <code>inline-start</code> or <code>inline-end</code>. <code>Side.Left</code> and <code>Side.Right</code> stay where they are.
        See the <a href="/docs/components/tooltip#rtl">Tooltip</a> and <a href="/docs/components/popover#rtl">Popover</a> examples.
    </p>
    <p>
        Sheet, Drawer and Sidebar sides are physical. Pick the side for the direction, as the
        <a href="/docs/components/sheet#rtl">Sheet</a> and <a href="/docs/components/sidebar#rtl">Sidebar</a> examples do.
    </p>

    <DocsHeading Title="Icons" />
    <p>
        Icons that point along the line, like <code>ArrowRight</code> or <code>ChevronLeft</code>, need <code>rtl:rotate-180</code> to point the right
        way. The components that ship one already have it. Add it to your own:
    </p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@IconCode" />

    <DocsHeading Title="Font Recommendations" />
    <p>
        Use a font that covers your language. <a href="https://fonts.google.com/noto">Noto</a> has Arabic, Hebrew and Persian families, and it
        pairs well with Inter and Geist.
    </p>

    <DocsHeading Title="Migrating existing components" />
    <Steps>
        <Step>Run the migrate command</Step>
        <CliCommand Args="migrate rtl [path]" />
        <p>
            <code>[path]</code> is a file or a folder to migrate. Without one, it migrates the files in <code>componentsDir</code>. It also sets
            <code>"rtl": true</code>, so components you add later come migrated.
        </p>
        <p>Run it once: a second run adds the <code>rtl:</code> classes again.</p>
        <Step>Check the components it lists</Step>
        <p>
            <code>Sidebar.razor</code>, <code>Pagination.razor</code> and <code>Calendar.razor</code> may need a look: pick the sidebar&apos;s side for the
            direction, and check that the pagination and calendar chevrons point the right way.
        </p>
        <Step>Turn your own icons around</Step>
        <p>Add <code>rtl:rotate-180</code> to the directional icons in your own markup. See <a href="#icons">Icons</a>.</p>
    </Steps>
</DocsPage>

@code {
    private const string HtmlCode = """
        <!DOCTYPE html>
        <html lang="ar" dir="rtl">
        <head>
            ...
        </head>
        <body>
            <Routes />
            <script src="_framework/blazor.web.js"></script>
        </body>
        </html>
        """;

    private const string ProviderCode = """
        <DirectionProvider Direction="TextDirection.Rtl">
            <Router AppAssembly="typeof(Program).Assembly">
                ...
            </Router>
        </DirectionProvider>
        """;

    private const string IconCode = """
        <Button Variant="ButtonVariant.Outline">
            Next
            <ArrowRight class="rtl:rotate-180" data-icon="inline-end" />
        </Button>
        """;
}
